# crud — the OLTP home turf (report-class; SQLite's strong regime, benched to lose honestly)

Seed 1. One shared op stream per family, folded by both engines; the read query oracle-gated (value-identical multisets) on every lane before any timed window. ratio = ours p50 / sqlite p50 (lower is better; <1 = bumbledb faster).

## lane durable

Db::create (LMDB issues F_FULLFSYNC unconditionally on macOS) vs SQLite WAL synchronous=FULL fullfsync=ON checkpoint_fullfsync=ON, cache_size=-262144, temp_store=MEMORY, whole-file mmap (coverage asserted), wal_autocheckpoint=0 — both engines flush to media on every commit

| family | about | ours p50 (µs) | sqlite p50 (µs) | ratio | ours p99 (µs) | sqlite p99 (µs) |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| crud_read_point | keyed point read: (id, val) by key, 3 hits + 1 miss rotation | 0.71 | 1.79 | 0.40 | 0.79 | 1.96 |
| crud_insert | one fresh Doc row per commit (fsync-bound single-writer floor) | 4916.38 | 4271.62 | 1.15 | 6256.54 | 5290.21 |
| crud_insert_10 | 10 fresh Doc rows per commit | 5156.12 | 4275.00 | 1.21 | 6702.92 | 5910.96 |
| crud_insert_100 | 100 fresh Doc rows per commit | 8418.25 | 4215.75 | 2.00 | 10097.25 | 5259.79 |
| crud_insert_1k | 1000 fresh Doc rows per commit | 19496.71 | 5030.38 | 3.88 | 21174.21 | 5274.62 |
| crud_update | one keyed Counter value replacement per commit | 4585.46 | 4165.54 | 1.10 | 6276.50 | 5246.08 |
| crud_update_hot | the same replacement pinned to one hot row (key 0 every sample) | 5051.08 | 4621.54 | 1.09 | 6243.42 | 5308.12 |
| crud_upsert | keyed upsert over twice the Counter mass (~half miss) | 5031.25 | 4225.04 | 1.19 | 6138.29 | 5264.21 |
| crud_rmw | read-modify-write round trip: point read, host +1, write back | 5060.08 | 4164.71 | 1.21 | 6204.92 | 6156.21 |
| crud_delete | one pool-row delete per commit (delete-bearing by contract) | 4944.33 | 4179.42 | 1.18 | 7610.88 | 6163.54 |
| crud_mixed_90_10 | 9 point reads + 1 single-row insert commit per sample | 5059.33 | 4236.67 | 1.19 | 8016.12 | 7146.46 |

## lane nosync

Db::ephemeral (MDB_NOSYNC: pages and meta pwritten, no sync boundary ever crossed) vs SQLite WAL synchronous=OFF fullfsync=OFF checkpoint_fullfsync=OFF, cache_size=-262144, temp_store=MEMORY, whole-file mmap (coverage asserted), wal_autocheckpoint=0 — WAL frames written, never synced (OFF, not NORMAL: NORMAL still syncs at checkpoints, which would cross-match a store kind that never syncs)

| family | about | ours p50 (µs) | sqlite p50 (µs) | ratio | ours p99 (µs) | sqlite p99 (µs) |
|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| crud_read_point | keyed point read: (id, val) by key, 3 hits + 1 miss rotation | 0.50 | 1.21 | 0.41 | 0.62 | 1.33 |
| crud_insert | one fresh Doc row per commit (fsync-bound single-writer floor) | 30.46 | 16.33 | 1.86 | 51.42 | 33.50 |
| crud_insert_10 | 10 fresh Doc rows per commit | 83.62 | 22.46 | 3.72 | 116.62 | 85.29 |
| crud_insert_100 | 100 fresh Doc rows per commit | 563.04 | 113.04 | 4.98 | 714.21 | 181.88 |
| crud_insert_1k | 1000 fresh Doc rows per commit | 4674.29 | 737.04 | 6.34 | 5277.58 | 833.92 |
| crud_update | one keyed Counter value replacement per commit | 32.00 | 10.12 | 3.16 | 41.12 | 67.04 |
| crud_update_hot | the same replacement pinned to one hot row (key 0 every sample) | 28.54 | 9.62 | 2.97 | 32.67 | 13.67 |
| crud_upsert | keyed upsert over twice the Counter mass (~half miss) | 27.29 | 15.17 | 1.80 | 36.00 | 50.88 |
| crud_rmw | read-modify-write round trip: point read, host +1, write back | 30.00 | 10.29 | 2.91 | 40.33 | 15.46 |
| crud_delete | one pool-row delete per commit (delete-bearing by contract) | 26.04 | 16.54 | 1.57 | 34.75 | 37.42 |
| crud_mixed_90_10 | 9 point reads + 1 single-row insert commit per sample | 31.54 | 27.79 | 1.13 | 37.75 | 61.25 |

post-state: Doc + Counter value-identical across engines, both lanes. Every row above is report-class, never gated — no budget gate reads a crud number.
